    ],
    "text": "GAME: A Seer on Fungi Living Strategies and"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000010",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0010-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Biodiversity Based on Gause\u2019s Model"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000011",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0002",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0002-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u516c\u4f17\u53f7\uff1a\u6570\u5b66\u6a21\u578b"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000012",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "heading",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0011-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Summary"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000013",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0012-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0012-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0012-l0000",
      "p0001-n0012-l0001",
      "p0001-n0012-l0002",
      "p0001-n0012-l0003",
      "p0001-n0012-l0004",
      "p0001-n0012-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Decomposition of organic matters by fungi, an indispensable part of carbon cycle, can make carbon reused in the environment. A recent article explores the impact of different traits on its decomposition effeciency. In this paper, we focus on two main traits, hyphal extension rate and moisture tolerance, together with interactions among fungi and various environmental conditions, to simulate the breakdown of woody \ufb01bers and comprehend the importance of biodiversity."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000014",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0001"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0000",
      "p0001-n0013-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Our GAME model is made up of the initials of four task names. Before we start our ex- periments, we build up a prediction model to simulate the cross action among different fungi"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000015",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "title",
    "repairs": [],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0003-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "\u5fae\u4fe1\u53f7\uff1aMATHmodels"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000016",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0013-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0013-l0005"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0013-l0002",
      "p0001-n0013-l0003",
      "p0001-n0013-l0004",
      "p0001-n0013-l0005"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "and their effect on the decomposition process of woody \ufb01bers. We adopt Gause\u2019s Compet- itive Model to uncover the interactions among species and derive a differential system by considering the change of woody \ufb01bers amount. The model describes growth, hyphal ex- tension, competition, and decomposition of fungi."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000017",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0014-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0014-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0014-l0000",
      "p0001-n0014-l0001",
      "p0001-n0014-l0002",
      "p0001-n0014-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Firstly, in order to simplify the model, we \ufb01x temperature T = 22 \u25e6C, and set the trait parameters of three different fungi arti\ufb01cially. Experiment results shown that our model is of high reasonability since the predicted decomposition rate is nearly 30%, which approxi- mately equals to veri\ufb01ed research results."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000018",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0015-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0015-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0015-l0000",
      "p0001-n0015-l0001",
      "p0001-n0015-l0002",
      "p0001-n0015-l0003",
      "p0001-n0015-l0004",
      "p0001-n0015-l0005",
      "p0001-n0015-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Secondly, we are to choose \ufb01ve representitive fungi as our experiment objects, which are P.Flavidoalba.S., P.Hartigii.N., M.Tremellosus.N., P.Sangioneus.S., and H.Setigerum.N., respectively. After describing their typical characteristics, we introduce the Moisture/Tem- perature Tolerance Factor for calibrating. Based on the model proposed, we \ufb01nd that the species P.Flavidoalba.S. is always dominant at Columbus (temperate) in short-term (7 days) and long-term (122 days), due to its general advantage on moisture. Also, rapid \ufb02uctuation experiment indicates those who adapt the environment well will be in dominance."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000019",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0003"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0003",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0004"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0004",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0005"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0016-l0005",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0016-l0006"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0016-l0000",
      "p0001-n0016-l0001",
      "p0001-n0016-l0002",
      "p0001-n0016-l0003",
      "p0001-n0016-l0004",
      "p0001-n0016-l0005",
      "p0001-n0016-l0006"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Thirdly, we choose \ufb01ve cities, Santa Fe (Arid), Sioux Falls (semi-arid), Columbus (tem- perate), Atlanta (arboreal), and Codaj\u00b4as (rain forest), and do the same prediction on the previous step. The result shows that, except for the leading fungus P.Flavidoalba.S., other species\u2019 density gradually decrease, but never tend to 0. Additionally, P.Flavidoalba.S., P.Sangioneus.S., M.Tremellosus.N. will have a consistent competition in tropical rain for- est, since they have their unique advantages in this environment. The decomposition rate will be relatively better for higher temperature and moisture to some extent."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000020",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0002"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0017-l0002",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0017-l0003"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0017-l0000",
      "p0001-n0017-l0001",
      "p0001-n0017-l0002",
      "p0001-n0017-l0003"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "Fourthly, we explore the decomposition ef\ufb01ciency of the system by changing the number of fungus, and discover that they actually have positive correlation in all areas. Moreover, it is shown that compared with arid region, tropical rain forest will have a higher requirement for biodiversity since it has a relatively stable climate."
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000021",
    "issues": [
      "hyphen_join_review"
    ],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0001"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0001-n0018-l0001",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0001-n0018-l0002"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0003",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0001-n0018-l0000",
      "p0001-n0018-l0001",
      "p0001-n0018-l0002"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      1
    ],
    "text": "After modelling, we also conduct sensitivity analysis, which reveals our model\u2019s robust- ness to some parameters. We \ufb01nally summarize our strengths and weaknesses. A brief conclusion is also presented in the paper."
  },
  {
